    "summary": "Model completed successfully after one repair round.\n\nRoot cause of the earlier failure: an instance data error. The girder section field girder.section.t_top was written as 0.20 m, but the description states the top slab is 0.18 m thick. The accepted section-property decisions (girder.single.A = 1.0605 m², girder.single.I = 0.25166 m⁴) had in fact been computed with 0.18 m, so the instance and the decision set were inconsistent, which the model checks flagged (suspect_decisions empty because the fault lay in the instance layer). Fix: corrected t_top to 0.18 m via write_instance; no decisions needed withdrawing or revising, and generate_model then passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nFinal model: single simply supported span, 25 m centre-to-centre of bearings, deck 16 m / carriageway 15 m, one-way, 4 design lanes, Highway Class II (JTG D60-2015). Five precast prestressed small-box girders per span (C40, self-weight only). Supports: abutments at both ends on plain laminated elastomeric bearings, 10 per line (two per girder end), 300×350 mm, 4 × 8 mm rubber layers, modelled as vertical + longitudinal springs with free rotation.\n\nKey results:\n- Vertical bending frequencies: f1 = 4.272 Hz (χ/μ = 0.2409 from JTGD60-4.3.2 applied).\n- Self-weight support reactions: 1723.3 kN per abutment.\n- Self-weight midspan moment: 10 770.9 kN·m.\n- Lane-load max positive moment (span 1): 6878.4 kN·m."
